    "notes": [
      "This table is from the user-provided images of Table 6.23: Building Height with respect to road width.",
      "* 70 mts height may be permitted on 18 mts and wider road within High Density Development area, i.e. 200 mts from the outer boundary of the road. High Density Development means an area where maximum permissible FSI is more than 3.5 in D1 except GMC and D2.",
      "** For DW1 and DW2 type residential buildings, maximum permissible building height shall be 12.0 mts.",
      "*** Note for Shamlaji Area Development Authority: (a) In Commercial-1 zone proposed around Shamlaji Vishnu Temple within TP Scheme-1 in Shamlaji Village, maximum permissible building height shall not exceed 10.0 mts (Ground + 2 floors). (b) In Special Zone-5 proposed around Shamlaji Vishnu Temple within TP Scheme-1 in Shamlaji Village, maximum permissible building height shall not exceed 13.0 mts (Ground + 3 floors)."
    ],
